269
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:49,520
I guess I should eat, too.

270
00:16:49,940 --> 00:16:50,300
Yeah.

271
00:16:51,740 --> 00:16:53,280
Come to mama, you.

272
00:16:54,040 --> 00:16:55,700
I should make this sometime.

273
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:59,620
It's a nice change from the more traditional Japanese food we usually eat at home.

274
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:03,620
Kitagawa must really love...

275
00:17:04,360 --> 00:17:05,280
fried rice.

276
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:14,560
Even if that's true, I'll never give up.

277
00:17:15,120 --> 00:17:16,820
Cause I'm a flower princess!

278
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:22,420
You can do it.

279
00:17:22,820 --> 00:17:24,620
Me right here.

280
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:26,280
Need some tissues?

281
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:27,340
I got you.

282
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:31,140
Hi, it's Gojo.

283
00:17:31,140 --> 00:17:34,540
I just wanted to check in on the multi-view sketch I sent.

284
00:17:35,180 --> 00:17:36,540
Anything you want me to revise?

285
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:37,240
No.

286
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:38,120
It's great.

287
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:39,280
Thank you.

288
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:39,900
I'm glad.

289
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:43,960
But hey, are your sketches always this detailed?

290
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:45,680
Uh, pretty much.

291
00:17:46,060 --> 00:17:47,480
Oh, that's impressive.

292
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:50,280
I can go ahead and send funds for the fabric.

293
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,340
How much do you think you'll need?

294
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:55,340
Oh, I'm not quite sure yet.

295
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:57,640
Would you be willing to wait until it's complete to pay?

296
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,880
I promise I'll do my best to keep the cost down.

297
00:18:00,220 --> 00:18:01,820
Oh, no problem.

298
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:02,880
I can do that.

299
00:18:03,160 --> 00:18:04,720
Do you want me to take care of hair and makeup?

300
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:06,500
Nah, don't worry about it.

301
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:07,620
I can do that myself.

302
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:08,880
Sounds like a plan.

303
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:13,880
But speaking of, I went through all your cosplay photos and I wanted to pick your brain about something.

304
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:15,120
Uh, sure.

305
00:18:15,540 --> 00:18:16,100
Go ahead.

306
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:16,900
Thanks.

307
00:18:17,540 --> 00:18:19,280
So I know how to reshape the eyelid.

308
00:18:20,080 --> 00:18:24,140
But for some of these characters, the shape of your eyes looks totally different overall.

309
00:18:24,860 --> 00:18:25,880
How do you pull that off?

310
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:26,900
Oh.

311
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:28,500
I use face tape.

312
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:29,640
Face tape?

313
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,700
Here, let me turn my camera on.

314
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:32,180
Oh.

315
00:18:32,180 --> 00:18:34,360
Can you see me?

316
00:18:34,860 --> 00:18:35,120
Yeah.

317
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:36,120
Crystal clear.

318
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:38,100
I use this.

319
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:41,100
Cosplay tape can totally change your look if you place it right.

320
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:48,020
For example, if you want your eyes to look bigger, anchor your tape mid-forehead or above each eye and pull it back over your wig cap.

321
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:50,100
You'll look more bright-eyed and doll-like.

322
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:51,900
And you won't have to think about it.

323
00:18:52,540 --> 00:18:52,940
Wow.

324
00:18:53,780 --> 00:18:57,080
Some cosplayers will use tape to sharpen their cheekbones or jawline.

325
00:18:57,580 --> 00:18:59,760
But you get the most bang for your buck like this.

326
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:02,460
Matching a character's eye shape is always a great detail.

327
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:05,740
We could have made Shizuku-tan look more droopy-eyed that way.

328
00:19:06,100 --> 00:19:06,620
Thank you.

329
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:07,700
This is really informative.

330
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:09,520
You've really never heard of this?

331
00:19:09,840 --> 00:19:10,220
No.

332
00:19:10,820 --> 00:19:12,520
That was my first cosplay experience.

333
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:13,760
You're kidding, right?

334
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:15,000
That outfit?

335
00:19:15,200 --> 00:19:16,920
That was your first time making one?

336
00:19:17,180 --> 00:19:17,520
Yeah.

337
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,000
I still have a lot to learn, obviously.

338
00:19:21,220 --> 00:19:26,120
I guess that explains why Kitakawa's photos were taken with a smartphone rather than a real camera.

339
00:19:27,660 --> 00:19:28,920
I don't get you.

340
00:19:29,760 --> 00:19:31,760
You're so...

341
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:32,760
Okay.

342
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:36,320
We should maybe plan on taking photos with our camera.

343
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:37,380
Wait, whose?

344
00:19:37,900 --> 00:19:39,540
Oh, did I not mention this?

345
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:42,040
My little sister is the one who takes my photos.

346
00:19:42,300 --> 00:19:43,420
Oh, that's cool.

347
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:46,140
Your sisters are really incredible photographer.

348
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:48,200
The colors in all of these are amazing.

349
00:19:48,640 --> 00:19:51,220
Well, we do finish them with photo editing software.

350
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:54,060
That way we can touch up blemishes or even perfect eye color.

351
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:55,200
Still incredible.

352
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:58,400
You guys should totally invest in a nice camera, too.

353
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:00,320
Um, Inui?

354
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:00,960
What?

355
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:05,600
If it's not too much trouble, could your sister give me a crash course in cameras?

356
00:20:05,980 --> 00:20:07,520
There's so much I don't know yet.

357
00:20:07,940 --> 00:20:08,320
Probably.

358
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:13,960
But she is still in middle school, and if we meet all the way out at your place, we wouldn't get home till late.

359
00:20:14,180 --> 00:20:15,700
I would be happy to meet you somewhere.

360
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:16,780
Okay.

361
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:20,640
There's a family restaurant near my place if that works for you.

362
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:22,440
Yes, that's perfectly fine.

363
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:23,380
Cool.

364
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:24,020
I'll text you.

365
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:24,580
Great.

366
00:20:25,280 --> 00:20:26,380
Thanks so much, Inui.

367
00:20:29,580 --> 00:20:30,780
A camera, huh?

368
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:34,060
There were a lot of fancy-looking ones at the event we went to.

369
00:20:39,700 --> 00:20:40,280
Yes, hello?

370
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:41,600
I want to come with you!

371
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:45,160
I'd love to learn how to use a real camera for this stuff.

372
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:46,180
Uh, sure.

373
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:47,820
Just let me ask Inui first.

374
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:49,220
Thanks, bud.

375
00:20:50,100 --> 00:20:54,140
Maureen, if I don't put food in me right now, I'm literally gonna die.

376
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:54,980
Be right there, Noah.

377
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:56,680
Go get us a table, okay?

378
00:20:57,760 --> 00:21:01,200
I had no idea Juju had a little sis.

379
00:21:01,660 --> 00:21:02,760
I bet she's way cute.

380
00:21:03,100 --> 00:21:07,180
Like a total clone of Juju, but a little teeny tiny baby version.

381
00:21:07,660 --> 00:21:09,880
Yeah, I can definitely picture that.

382
00:21:09,880 --> 00:21:12,820
I'm so freaking excited now!

383
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:17,860
It's very nice to meet you.

384
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:19,080
Hey, don't slouch.

385
00:21:19,360 --> 00:21:20,200
Come on, sit up.

386
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:21,400
Okay, sorry.

387
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:24,440
She always gets nervous when she meets new people.

388
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:27,380
I, uh...

389
00:21:27,380 --> 00:21:27,880
I'm...

390
00:21:28,680 --> 00:21:30,120
I'm Shinju Inui.

391
00:21:30,120 --> 00:21:34,600
And it's a pleasure to make your acquaintance.

392
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,180
Well, she's certainly not what I pictured.

393
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:44,120
And she's...

394
00:21:45,280 --> 00:21:47,240
She's in middle school?

395
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:48,360
Oh my god, girl!

396
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:50,820
Like, I dreamed of being that huge in middle school.

397
00:21:51,080 --> 00:21:52,360
Just how big are you?

398
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:53,160
Uh...

399
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:53,920
Kitagawa!

400
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:56,060
I'm five four and a half on a good day.

401
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:58,580
I'm, um...

402
00:21:58,580 --> 00:21:59,980
I'm five foot ten?

403
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:00,600
No way!

404
00:22:00,740 --> 00:22:01,440
Shut up!

405
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:02,720
I am so jealous!

406
00:22:02,900 --> 00:22:04,180
Of course that's what she meant.

407
00:22:04,180 --> 00:22:16,100
Outro Music

408
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:25,960
I

409
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:55,940
Thank you.

410
00:22:55,960 --> 00:23:25,940
Thank you.

411
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:55,940
Thank you.

